       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks like it may be an error.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** Metformin immediate-release is capped at 2,550 mg/day, usually given as up to 850 mg three times daily. The extended-release maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The ordered amount is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what you intended.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Something else.** If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was confirmed intentionally.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
